---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

// Covers use of the WEBSITE only. Actual landscaping work is governed by the
// written estimate/agreement signed for that job — this page must never read as
// a service guarantee or as terms for the work itself (brand guardrails).
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of Service · ${site.legalName}`}
  description={`The terms that apply to using the ${site.legalName} website.`}
>
  <LegalPage title="Terms of Service" updated="September 18, 2026">
    <p>
      These terms apply to this website, operated by <strong>{site.legalName}</strong> ("we," "us").
      By using the site you're agreeing to them. They're short on purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      This site describes the work we do and gives you a way to ask for an estimate. Everything here
      is general information about our services — it isn't a quote, a price list, or an offer to do
      work at any particular price.
    </p>

    <h2>Requesting an estimate</h2>
    <p>
      Submitting the quote form starts a conversation. It doesn't create a contract, hold a spot on
      our schedule, or obligate either of us to anything. We'll follow up to talk through the project
      and, if it's a fit, put together an estimate.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The work itself is governed by the written estimate or agreement we sign for that
      job</strong> — scope, price, timeline, and terms all live there. If anything on this website
      appears to conflict with that agreement, the signed agreement controls.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please give us accurate contact and property information. We rely on it to reach you and to
      understand the site we'd be working on.
    </p>

    <h2>Photos and content</h2>
    <p>
      The project photography on this site is of real work by our crew. The text, photographs, logo,
      and design are ours (or used with permission) and are protected by copyright. You're welcome to
      view and share links to the site. Please don't copy the photography or content for your own
      commercial use without asking us first.
    </p>

    <h2>Reviews and ratings</h2>
    <p>
      Any reviews or ratings shown here were written by customers and are reproduced as they were
      given. They describe those customers' own projects. Every property is different, and someone
      else's experience isn't a promise about yours.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>
      Don't use this site to break the law, to submit false information or someone else's contact
      details, to send automated or bulk submissions through the form, or to try to interfere with
      how the site runs.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We keep the site accurate and current as best we can, but we don't warrant that it's free of
      errors or always available. Service descriptions, service areas, and availability can change.
      The site is provided "as is," without warranties of any kind, to the fullest extent the law
      allows.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, we aren't liable for indirect, incidental, or
      consequential damages arising from your use of this website. Nothing in this section limits our
      responsibilities under a signed agreement for work we perform, or any liability that can't be
      limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Where we link to another site, we don't control it and aren't responsible for its content or
      its privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      How we handle the information you send through this site is covered in our{" "}
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed, and the current
      version is always the one on this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of North Carolina, without regard to its
      conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute about this website belongs in the state or federal courts
      serving Orange County, North Carolina.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Phone: <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a></li>
      {site.email && <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>}
      <li>{site.legalName}, {site.areas[0]}, {site.region} {site.zip}</li>
    </ul>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
